### === AUTH ===

### 1. Request magic link code (creates user if not exists)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/magic/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com"
}

###

### 2. Verify code and get Bearer token
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/magic/verify-login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "code": "123456"
}

###

### 3. Logout (invalidate current token)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/magic/logout
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### 4. Logout all devices
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/magic/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### 5. List active sessions
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/sessions
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### 6. Revoke a specific session
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/sessions/1
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### 7. Login history (cursor-based pagination)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/login-history?limit=50
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###


### === USERS ===

### 8. Get current user
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### 9. Update current user
PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer <token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newemail@example.com"
}

###

### 10. Get user by ID (superuser only)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/users/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### 11. Update user by ID (superuser only)
PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/users/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer <token>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "is_active": true
}

###

### 12. Delete user (superuser only)
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/users/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###
